body:
This issue is reproducible with devstral or deepcoder served on local ollama.

Edited file contains following code:
```
    // Load mock responses from JSON files
    async function loadMockResponses() {
        const responses = {
            nodes: await import('./resources/nodes.json'),
            namespaces: await import('./resources/namespaces.json'),
        };
        return responses;
    }
```

In the cline UI I see a message "Cline wants to edit this file:" with this dropdown output:
```
<<<<<<< SEARCH
    // Load mock responses from JSON files
    async function loadMockResponses() {
        const responses = {
            nodes: await import('./resources/nodes.json'),
            namespaces: await import('./resources/namespaces.json'),
        };
        return responses;
    }
>>>>>>> RE
```


It looks like the last word "REPLACE" is cut, probably it is not expected by cline.

```
<replace_in_file>
<path>mock/-js-mock-kubernets-api-client.js</path>
<diff>
<<<<<<< SEARCH
    // Load mock responses from JSON files
    async function loadMockResponses() {
        const responses = {
            nodes: await import('./resources/nodes.json'),
            namespaces: await import('./resources/namespaces.json'),
        };
        return responses;
    }
<<<<<<< REPLACE
    // Load mock responses from JSON files synchronously
    function loadMockResponses() {
        const responses = {
            nodes: JSON.parse(FileSystem.readFile('./resources/nodes.json')),
            namespaces: JSON.parse(FileSystem.readFile('./resources/namespaces.json')),
        };
        return responses;
>>>>>>> REPLACE
====

[Response interrupted by a tool use result. Only one tool may be used at a time and should be placed at the end of the message.]

```

UPDATE: I have fixed the issue by providing additional example in Custom Instructions of Cline Settings:

```
Format of code to make targeted edit to a file (e.g. rename a function parameter from "name" to "userName")

<replace_in_file>
<path>src/logic.js</path>
<diff>
<<<<<<< SEARCH
var fnc = function (name) {
=======
var fnc = function (userName) {
>>>>>>> REPLACE

</diff>
</replace_in_file>
```

It looks like the system prompt of Cline is huge, and the SEARCH REPLACE instructions are somewhere in the middle. The local models are kind of struggling to follow this instructions, if a lot of other instructions aloe exist. With an additional example, that is placed by custom instuctions at the end of the system prompt, the instruction seem to be effective.
